WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:02.790
- [Narrator] This rail bridge
is the only border crossing

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.890
between Russia and North Korea.

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:05.723
In early November,

00:00:05.723 --> 00:00:08.340
satellite imagery showed a
train crossing into Russia.

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:11.220
The first movement
observed there in years.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.053
In the past,

00:00:12.053 --> 00:00:14.400
the railway was used to
transport passengers and goods,

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:16.410
but Russia and North Korea
didn't return our questions

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.390
on what the train was carrying this time.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:19.830
It is one sign of renewed activity

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:21.090
between the two countries,

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:24.030
which have indicated a desire
to expand their partnership.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.980
Their leaders have exchanged letters,

00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:27.150
Russia said it recently sent

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.070
thoroughbred horses to North Korea,

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:30.450
and Pyongyang is even looking to help

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.700
rebuild parts of Ukraine.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.155
But US Intelligence says
the cooperation is deeper

00:00:35.155 --> 00:00:35.988
(missiles swooshing)

00:00:35.988 --> 00:00:38.040
and that Pyongyang is
selling arms to Moscow.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.260
This would go against
United Nations sanctions,

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:42.870
and both countries deny the reports.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:43.703
So here's what we know

00:00:43.703 --> 00:00:46.233
about how the two isolated
nations are growing closer.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.640
Putin and Kim haven't
officially met since 2019,

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.340
but they've exchanged at
least six letters this year.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.810
Both leaders have regularly mentioned

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.460
the cooperation between the two countries

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.998
that's never been stronger.

00:00:57.998 --> 00:01:00.330
(speaking Russian)

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:01.710
- [Narrator] Pyongyang
has been the only capital

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:03.720
to recognize Moscow's sham referendums

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.010
that paved the way for the Kremlin

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:06.840
to claim occupied Ukrainian regions

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:09.180
as part of the Russian Federation.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.610
On its end, Russia has
blocked Washington led efforts

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.800
to enforce additional
sanctions on North Korea

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.023
after a recent barrage
of missile launches.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:18.960
North Korea is also looking to help Moscow

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.660
on the ground in Ukraine.

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:23.577
(speaking Russian)

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.260
- [Narrator] In July, North
Korea's Ambassador to Russia

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.093
met with an official

00:01:29.093 --> 00:01:31.020
from the Russian occupied Donetsk Republic

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:32.970
discussing joint projects in construction,

00:01:32.970 --> 00:01:35.310
agriculture, and other sectors.

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:36.720
There is no evidence that North Koreans

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.400
are working in the occupied territories,

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.660
which would violate the UN ban

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.640
on the use of North Korean Labor.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:42.840
Russian officials said they looked into

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.520
how to employ North Korean workers

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.473
without breaching UN resolutions.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.550
Those international
sanctions also affect goods,

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.020
including arms sales.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:57.020
- The DPRK is covertly supplying

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.650
Russia with a significant
number of artillery shells.

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.420
- [Narrator] The Democratic
People's Republic of Korea,

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:05.850
or DPRK, is being accused by the US

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:07.110
of using a network of countries

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:08.730
in the Middle East and North Africa

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.458
to send ammunition to Russian forces.

00:02:11.458 --> 00:02:12.291
(tanks blasting)

00:02:12.291 --> 00:02:13.410
Pyongyang is a major producer of arms,

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:15.090
holding large stockpiles.

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:16.920
Much of it is based on
Soviet era technology

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:19.080
and is very similar to Russian weapons.

00:02:19.080 --> 00:02:20.850
All this, North Korea watchers say,

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:23.310
makes it an attractive source
of ammunition for Russia,

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.540
although trade of the two countries

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.853
is heavily restricted
by a slew of sanctions.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.250
Some Western officials have assessed

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.870
that Russia is running
through its arsenal,

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:32.250
as military experts estimate

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:34.983
it fires approximately
20,000 shells per day.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:37.230
As Russia grows more isolated,

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:39.150
it's looking for any help it can get.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:41.250
The resumption of the train
traffic with North Korea,

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.650
suspended during the
pandemic, shows how Moscow

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.690
is looking to work with
its eastern neighbor.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:47.190
And experts on North Korea and Russia

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:49.200
agree that the two countries
will only grow closer

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.480
as Russia seeks support for its war.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:52.350
And North Korea,

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.810
which has been particularly
isolated in recent years,

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.540
could also benefit from a
stronger alliance with Moscow,

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.703
both politically and economically.

